From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Makefile: touch only existing LuCI paths in postinst and
 postupgrade

Package/tachyon/postinst and postupgrade refresh the LuCI cache with
`touch luci.js view/tachyon resources`. touch on a missing path creates
an empty file. When tachyon is installed or upgraded without
luci-app-tachyon on the router (it comes later in the same apk
transaction, or is installed later), /www/luci-static/resources/view/tachyon
becomes a plain file, and luci-app-tachyon then fails to install with
"Not a directory". The author fixed the same lines in build.sh (the
release packages); the Makefile used by buildroot and SDK builds still
had them.

Each path is now touched only if it exists, as in build.sh. A plain
file at view/tachyon, left by such an install, is removed, so
luci-app-tachyon can be installed again. Image builds are not affected:
both scripts exit early when IPKG_INSTROOT is set.

diff --git a/tachyon/Makefile b/tachyon/Makefile
index 74dd4c60..14ce3c5f 100644
--- a/tachyon/Makefile
+++ b/tachyon/Makefile
@@ -174,9 +174,15 @@ for _comp in zapret zapret2 byedpi wdtt-client qwdtt olcrtc; do
 	fi
 done
 
-# LuCI cache touch invalidation
+# LuCI cache touch invalidation. Only paths that exist: touch on a missing one
+# creates an empty file, and a file in place of view/tachyon (this package can be
+# installed or upgraded before luci-app-tachyon) makes its install fail with
+# "Not a directory". Such a file left by an earlier build is removed.
+[ -f /www/luci-static/resources/view/tachyon ] && rm -f /www/luci-static/resources/view/tachyon 2>/dev/null || true
 for _f in /www/luci-static/resources/view/tachyon/*.js; do [ -f "$$_f" ] && touch "$$_f" 2>/dev/null || true; done
-touch /www/luci-static/resources/luci.js /www/luci-static/resources/view/tachyon /www/luci-static/resources 2>/dev/null || true
+for _p in /www/luci-static/resources/luci.js /www/luci-static/resources/view/tachyon /www/luci-static/resources; do
+	[ -e "$$_p" ] && touch "$$_p" 2>/dev/null || true
+done
 
 # Start via tachyon binary (lifecycle.uc) which registers with procd directly,
 # bypassing rc.common and its flock entirely.
@@ -309,9 +315,15 @@ TACHYON_LIB=/usr/lib/tachyon ucode -L /usr/lib/tachyon /usr/lib/tachyon/config/m
 
 /usr/bin/tachyon package_postinst
 
-# LuCI cache touch invalidation
+# LuCI cache touch invalidation. Only paths that exist: touch on a missing one
+# creates an empty file, and a file in place of view/tachyon (this package can be
+# installed or upgraded before luci-app-tachyon) makes its install fail with
+# "Not a directory". Such a file left by an earlier build is removed.
+[ -f /www/luci-static/resources/view/tachyon ] && rm -f /www/luci-static/resources/view/tachyon 2>/dev/null || true
 for _f in /www/luci-static/resources/view/tachyon/*.js; do [ -f "$$_f" ] && touch "$$_f" 2>/dev/null || true; done
-touch /www/luci-static/resources/luci.js /www/luci-static/resources/view/tachyon /www/luci-static/resources 2>/dev/null || true
+for _p in /www/luci-static/resources/luci.js /www/luci-static/resources/view/tachyon /www/luci-static/resources; do
+	[ -e "$$_p" ] && touch "$$_p" 2>/dev/null || true
+done
 
 # The rpcd ACL for this binary ships here rather than in luci-app-tachyon, so
 # the policy and the executable it governs are installed in the same package and
